rules.content:
# 规则概述
在嵌套语句后增加空行，以提高代码可读性和维护性。

## 规则意义
在嵌套语句后增加空行可以增强代码的可读性，使代码结构更加清晰，也有助于减少因为代码紧凑而导致的误解或错误。

## 错误示例
```csharp
if (x)
    Foo();
Bar();
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
if (x)
    Foo();

Bar();
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
Add a blank line after embedded statements to improve code readability and maintainability.

## Rule Meaning
Adding a blank line after embedded statements can enhance code readability, making the code structure clearer and helping to reduce misinterpretations or errors due to closely packed code.

## Error Example
```csharp
if (x)
    Foo();
Bar();
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
if (x)
    Foo();

Bar();
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
在 `#region` 指令后添加一个空行以提高代码可读性。

## 规则意义
在 `#region` 指令后插入空行能够增加代码的可读性，使代码结构更清晰，帮助开发者快速识别出代码的逻辑块。这是一种良好的编码习惯，有助于团队维护和代码审查。

## 错误示例
```csharp
class C
{
    #region Methods
    void M()
    {
    }

    #endregion
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
class C
{
    #region Methods

    void M()
    {
    }

    #endregion
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
Add a blank line after the `#region` directive to enhance code readability.

## Rule Meaning
Inserting a blank line after the `#region` directive can increase code readability and make the code structure clearer. It helps developers quickly identify the logical blocks of code. This is a good coding practice that aids in team maintenance and code review.

## Error Example
```csharp
class C
{
    #region Methods
    void M()
    {
    }

    #endregion
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
class C
{
    #region Methods

    void M()
    {
    }

    #endregion
}
```

