rules.content:
# 规则概述
在C#类或枚举中，当存在多行声明时，需要在每个声明之间加入一个空行，以提高代码的可读性。

## 规则意义
保持代码的清晰和可维护性，通过在声明间加入空行，开发人员可以更容易地理解代码结构，识别各部分功能，从而减少代码审查和维护的难度。

## 错误示例
```csharp
class Foo
{
    void M1()
    {
    }
    void M2()
    {
    }
    /// <summary>
    /// ...
    /// </summary>
    void M3()
    {
    }
    string P1 { get; set; }
    [Obsolete]
    string P2 { get; set; }
}
enum Bar
{
    A = 0,
    /// <summary>
    /// ...
    /// </summary>
    B = 1,
    [Obsolete]
    C = 2,
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
class Foo
{
    void M1()
    {
    }

    void M2()
    {
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// ...
    /// </summary>
    void M3()
    {
    }

    string P1 { get; set; }

    [Obsolete]
    string P2 { get; set; }
}

enum Bar
{
    A = 0,

    /// <summary>
    /// ...
    /// </summary>
    B = 1,

    [Obsolete]
    C = 2,
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In a C# class or enum, when there are multiple line declarations, add a blank line between each declaration to improve code readability.

## Rule Meaning
Maintaining the clarity and maintainability of the code is important. By adding blank lines between declarations, developers can more easily understand the code structure, recognize the functionality of each part, and thus reduce the difficulty of code review and maintenance.

## Error Example
```csharp
class Foo
{
    void M1()
    {
    }
    void M2()
    {
    }
    /// <summary>
    /// ...
    /// </summary>
    void M3()
    {
    }
    string P1 { get; set; }
    [Obsolete]
    string P2 { get; set; }
}
enum Bar
{
    A = 0,
    /// <summary>
    /// ...
    /// </summary>
    B = 1,
    [Obsolete]
    C = 2,
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
class Foo
{
    void M1()
    {
    }

    void M2()
    {
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// ...
    /// </summary>
    void M3()
    {
    }

    string P1 { get; set; }

    [Obsolete]
    string P2 { get; set; }
}

enum Bar
{
    A = 0,

    /// <summary>
    /// ...
    /// </summary>
    B = 1,

    [Obsolete]
    C = 2,
}
```

