rules.content:
# 规则概述
在switch语句的标签(case/default)后面添加新行，以提高代码可读性和可维护性。

## 规则意义
当所有的switch标签后的代码都放在同一行时，代码紧凑但可读性差，容易导致维护困难。通过在每个switch标签后添加一个新行，可以划分代码逻辑，提高代码的可读性和维护的便利性。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
switch (x)
{
    case "a": return A();
    case "b": return B();
}
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
switch (x)
{
    case "a":
        return A();
    case "b":
        return B();
}
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
Add a new line after the switch statement labels (case/default) to improve code readability and maintainability.

## Rule Meaning
When all code after switch labels is placed on the same line, it becomes compact but less readable, leading to maintenance difficulty. Adding a new line after each switch label can segment the code logic, enhancing the readability and ease of maintenance.

## Error Example
'''csharp
switch (x)
{
    case "a": return A();
    case "b": return B();
}
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
switch (x)
{
    case "a":
        return A();
    case "b":
        return B();
}
'''

rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则要求在属性的完整访问器上每个访问器都必须独占一行，以提高代码的可读性和一致性。

## 规则意义
在代码中将完整访问器放在单独的行上有助于提高代码的可读性，特别是在代码审查和协作开发中。这种风格的排列可以使得代码布局更加清晰，减少行内代码的拥挤。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
string Foo { get { return _foo; } set { _foo = value; } }
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
string Foo
{
    get { return _foo; }
    set { _foo = value; }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires each full accessor of a property to be on its own line to enhance code readability and consistency.

## Rule Meaning
Putting full accessors on their own lines improves readability of code, especially useful during code reviews and collaborative development. This style of arrangement makes the code layout clearer and reduces clutter in single lines of code.

## Error Example
'''csharp
string Foo { get { return _foo; } set { _foo = value; } }
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
string Foo
{
    get { return _foo; }
    set { _foo = value; }
}
'''

rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则建议将构造函数初始化器置于单独的行，以提高代码的可读性和维护性。

## 规则意义
在一个代码块中，保持一致的格式样式有助于开发者快速理解代码逻辑并减少误解的可能性。将构造函数初始化器放在单独的行可以使代码格式更加干净，易于维护。

## 错误示例
```csharp
Foo(object p1, object p2) : base(p1)
{
    P2 = p2;
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
Foo(object p1, object p2)
    : base(p1)
{
    P2 = p2;
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule suggests placing the constructor initializer on a separate line to improve the readability and maintainability of the code.

## Rule Meaning
Maintaining a consistent format style in a code block helps developers quickly understand the code logic and reduce the possibility of misunderstanding. Putting the constructor initializer on a separate line makes the code format cleaner and easier to maintain.

## Error Example
```csharp
Foo(object p1, object p2) : base(p1)
{
    P2 = p2;
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
Foo(object p1, object p2)
    : base(p1)
{
    P2 = p2;
}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
在C#代码中，'if'语句和紧随其后的'else'语句之间不应该存在换行符。这有助于保持代码的一致性和可读性。

## 规则意义
这个规则有助于规范代码格式，使代码在多个开发者之间保持一致，从而提高整体代码的可读性和可维护性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
if (x)
{
    Foo();
}
else
if (y)
{
    Bar();
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
if (x)
{
    Foo();
}
else if (y)
{
    Bar();
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In C# code, there should not be a newline between an 'if' statement and its subsequent 'else' statement. This helps maintain consistency and readability of the code.

## Rule Meaning
This rule helps to standardize code formatting, ensuring consistency across multiple developers, which improves overall code readability and maintainability.

## Error Example
```csharp
if (x)
{
    Foo();
}
else
if (y)
{
    Bar();
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
if (x)
{
    Foo();
}
else if (y)
{
    Bar();
}
```

rules.content:
