# 规则概述
此规则确保文件末尾的空白符号规范化：默认情况下，要求文件末尾有一个新行；如果选项 `roslynator.prefer_new_line_at_end_of_file` 设置为 `false`，则不要求末尾新行。

## 规则意义
文件末尾的空白符处理对于代码风格一致性和多平台代码共享非常重要。保持一致的空白符处理可以减少因开发环境不同导致的代码变更差异。

## 错误示例
```csharp
// 文件末尾没有新行
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}  

// 当选项 `roslynator.prefer_new_line_at_end_of_file` 为 false 时，文件末尾有不需要的新行
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}

```

## 正确示例
```csharp
// 文件末尾有一个新行
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}

// 当选项 `roslynator.prefer_new_line_at_end_of_file` 为 false 时，正确没有新行
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}

```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule ensures the normalization of whitespace at the end of a file: by default, it requires a new line at the end of a file; if the option `roslynator.prefer_new_line_at_end_of_file` is set to `false`, it does not require a new line.

## Rule Meaning
Handling whitespace at the end of files is important for consistent code style and code sharing across different platforms. Consistent whitespace handling reduces differences in code changes caused by differing development environments.

## Error Example
```csharp
// No newline at the end of the file
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}  

// When the option `roslynator.prefer_new_line_at_end_of_file` is false, an unnecessary newline exists
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}

```

## Correct Example
```csharp
// A newline exists at the end of the file
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}

// When the option `roslynator.prefer_new_line_at_end_of_file` is false, correctly no newline
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}

```

