# 规则概述
该规则建议在catch块中重新抛出异常时，直接使用`throw`而不是`throw ex;`。

## 规则意义
使用`throw ex;`会丢失原始异常的堆栈跟踪信息，这可能会导致在调试和日志记录时定位问题变得困难。直接使用`throw`可以保留异常的完整堆栈跟踪，提升代码可维护性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
try
{
    Foo();
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    throw ex;
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
try
{
    Foo();
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    throw;
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule recommends using `throw` instead of `throw ex;` when re-throwing an exception in a catch block.

## Rule Meaning
Using `throw ex;` causes the loss of the original exception's stack trace, which can make it difficult to debug and log issues. Using `throw` directly preserves the complete stack trace of the exception, improving code maintainability.

## Error Example
```csharp
try
{
    Foo();
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    throw ex;
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
try
{
    Foo();
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    throw;
}
```

