# 规则概述
异步方法的命名应该以 'Async' 后缀结束，以便于提高代码的可读性和一致性。

## 规则意义
在C#中，异步方法返回类型通常是 Task 或 Task&lt;T&gt;，这样的命名约定可以帮助开发者快速识别方法的异步特性，并将其与同步方法区分开来，从而减少误用的可能性。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
public static async Task&lt;bool&gt; Foo()
{
    return await Task.FromResult(false);
}
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
public static async Task&lt;bool&gt; FooAsync()
{
    return await Task.FromResult(false);
}
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
The naming of asynchronous methods should end with the 'Async' suffix to enhance code readability and consistency.

## Rule Meaning
In C#, asynchronous methods typically return Task or Task&lt;T&gt;; this naming convention helps developers to quickly identify the asynchronous nature of methods and distinguish them from synchronous ones, reducing the likelihood of misuse.

## Error Example
'''csharp
public static async Task&lt;bool&gt; Foo()
{
    return await Task.FromResult(false);
}
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
public static async Task&lt;bool&gt; FooAsync()
{
    return await Task.FromResult(false);
}
'''

rules.content:
