# 规则概述
此规则建议移除`switch`语句中不必要的`case`标签，以简化代码结构，提高代码可读性。

## 规则意义
在`switch`语句中，如果某个`case`标签会导致与`default`分支相同的行为，则该标签是多余的，可以安全移除。这样做可以使代码更简洁，减少阅读和维护的负担。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
switch (s)
{
    case "a":
        return true;
    case "b":
    default:
        return false;
}
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
switch (s)
{
    case "a":
        return true;
    default:
        return false;
}
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule suggests removing unnecessary `case` labels in `switch` statements to simplify code structure and improve readability.

## Rule Meaning
In a `switch` statement, if a `case` label results in the same behavior as the `default` branch, the label is redundant and can be safely removed. Doing so simplifies the code, reducing the burden of reading and maintenance.

## Error Example
'''csharp
switch (s)
{
    case "a":
        return true;
    case "b":
    default:
        return false;
}
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
switch (s)
{
    case "a":
        return true;
    default:
        return false;
}
'''

