# 规则概述
该规则建议使用`Count`或`Length`属性来代替`Any`方法，以优化代码性能。使用`Count > 0`或`Length > 0`可以避免不必要的方法调用，从而提升性能。

## 规则意义
许多情况下，使用`Count`或`Length`属性来检查集合是否为空会比调用`Any`方法更为高效。`Any`方法会进行一个函数调用，而`Count`或`Length`直接返回集合大小，开销更小。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
if (list.Any())
{
    // 逻辑代码
}
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
if (list.Count > 0)
{
    // 逻辑代码
}
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule suggests using the `Count` or `Length` property instead of the `Any` method to optimize code performance. Using `Count > 0` or `Length > 0` avoids unnecessary method calls and thus improves performance.

## Rule Meaning
In many cases, using the `Count` or `Length` property to check if a collection is empty is more efficient than calling the `Any` method. The `Any` method involves a function call, whereas `Count` or `Length` directly returns the size of the collection with less overhead.

## Error Example
'''csharp
if (list.Any())
{
    // logic code
}
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
if (list.Count > 0)
{
    // logic code
}
'''

