# 规则概述
该规则建议在所有成员均为静态成员的类上加上`static`修饰符。这可以提高代码的可读性，并明确表示该类不应实例化。

## 规则意义
通过将只包含静态成员的类标记为静态，可以避免错误地实例化该类。此外，这还可以传达类设计的意图，提高代码的可维护性和性能。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public class Foo
{
    private static string _f;

    public static void Bar()
    {
    }
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public static class Foo
{
    private static string _f;

    public static void Bar()
    {
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule suggests adding the `static` modifier to a class where all members are static. This enhances code readability and clearly indicates that the class should not be instantiated.

## Rule Meaning
By marking a class with only static members as static, we can avoid mistakenly instantiating the class. Additionally, this conveys the design intent of the class, improving code maintainability and performance.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class Foo
{
    private static string _f;

    public static void Bar()
    {
    }
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public static class Foo
{
    private static string _f;

    public static void Bar()
    {
    }
}
```

