# 规则概述
该规则旨在帮助开发者识别和简化不必要的复杂条件表达式，以提高代码可读性和可维护性。

## 规则意义
复杂和冗长的条件表达式可能会影响代码的可读性和理解性。通过简化条件表达式，可以使代码更加清晰和易于维护，同时也可能提高代码的执行效率。

## 错误示例
```csharp
bool x = y ? true : false;
bool x = y ? false : true;
bool x = y ? z : false;
bool x = y ? true : z;
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
bool x = y;
bool x = !y;
bool x = y && z;
bool x = y || z;
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule aims to help developers identify and simplify unnecessarily complex conditional expressions to improve code readability and maintainability.

## Rule Meaning
Complex and lengthy conditional expressions can affect code readability and comprehension. Simplifying conditional expressions can make code clearer and easier to maintain, which might also enhance execution efficiency.

## Error Example
```csharp
bool x = y ? true : false;
bool x = y ? false : true;
bool x = y ? z : false;
bool x = y ? true : z;
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
bool x = y;
bool x = !y;
bool x = y && z;
bool x = y || z;
```

