# 规则概述
在C#编程中，通常建议将类型声明放置在命名空间内，以提高代码结构的清晰性和可维护性。

## 规则意义
将类型声明放在命名空间内可以避免全局类型命名冲突，增强代码的模块化，并使代码更具可读性和组织性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public class Foo
{
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
namespace ExampleNamespace
{
    public class Foo
    {
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In C# programming, it is generally recommended to declare types inside namespaces to improve the clarity and maintainability of the code structure.

## Rule Meaning
Declaring types inside namespaces helps avoid global type name conflicts, enhances code modularity, and makes code more readable and organized.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class Foo
{
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
namespace ExampleNamespace
{
    public class Foo
    {
    }
}
```

