# 规则概述
该规则建议在必要的时候为表达式添加括号，以避免运算优先级误解导致的逻辑错误。

## 规则意义
添加括号使代码更具可读性，确保开发人员明确每个部分的执行顺序，尤其是在复杂表达式中，括号可以清晰地传达开发者的意图。

## 错误示例
```csharp
if (x || y && z)
{
}

x?.y!.z
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
if (x || (y && z))
{
}

(x?.y)!.z
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule suggests adding parentheses when necessary to prevent misunderstandings due to operator precedence, which may lead to logical errors.

## Rule Meaning
Using parentheses improves code readability and ensures that the execution order of each part is clear to developers. In complex expressions, parentheses can clearly convey the developer's intent.

## Error Example
```csharp
if (x || y && z)
{
}

x?.y!.z
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
if (x || (y && z))
{
}

(x?.y)!.z
```

