# 规则概述
在使用`using`语句的代码块中，手动调用`Dispose`或`Close`方法是多余的，因为`using`语句会自动处理这些资源的释放。

## 规则意义
减少不必要的代码，从而提升代码可读性并降低维护成本。

## 错误示例
```csharp
using (streamReader)
{
    // ...

    streamReader.Dispose();
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
using (streamReader)
{
    // ...
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
A `Dispose` or `Close` method call inside a `using` statement block is redundant because the `using` statement automatically handles resource disposal.

## Rule Meaning
Eliminating unnecessary code can improve readability and reduce maintenance cost.

## Error Example
```csharp
using (streamReader)
{
    // ...

    streamReader.Dispose();
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
using (streamReader)
{
    // ...
}
```

