# 规则概述
在方法中检查未约束的泛型类型参数时，不应直接与null进行比较，而应该使用`EqualityComparer<T>.Default`来进行等价性比较。

## 规则意义
这条规则有助于避免在处理没有空约束的泛型类型参数时出现错误或异常，提高代码的健壮性和可读性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public void Foo<T1>() where T1 : new()
{
    var x = default(T1);

    if (x == null)
    {
        // 错误：直接检查泛型类型参数是否等于null
    }
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public void Foo<T1>() where T1 : new()
{
    var x = default(T1);

    if (EqualityComparer<T1>.Default.Equals(x, default(T1)))
    {
        // 正确：使用EqualityComparer进行等价性比较
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
When checking for null on unconstrained generic type parameters, you should not compare them directly with null. Instead, use `EqualityComparer<T>.Default` to perform the equality check.

## Rule Meaning
This rule helps to avoid potential errors or exceptions when dealing with unconstrained generic type parameters, thus improving the robustness and readability of the code.

## Error Example
```csharp
public void Foo<T1>() where T1 : new()
{
    var x = default(T1);

    if (x == null)
    {
        // Error: Directly checking if a generic type parameter is null
    }
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public void Foo<T1>() where T1 : new()
{
    var x = default(T1);

    if (EqualityComparer<T1>.Default.Equals(x, default(T1)))
    {
        // Correct: Using EqualityComparer for equality check
    }
}
```

