{
    return await GetAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public static Task<object> FooAsync()
{
    return GetAsync();
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule checks and removes unnecessary usage of `async` and `await`, thus simplifying the code and improving its execution efficiency.

## Rule Meaning
In certain situations, using `async` and `await` introduces unnecessary overhead. When an `async` method merely returns the result of an asynchronous operation without performing any additional asynchronous operations or error handling, `async` and `await` are redundant. Removing them can enhance performance and reduce code complexity.

## Error Example
```csharp
public static async Task<object> FooAsync()
{
    return await GetAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public static Task<object> FooAsync()
{
    return GetAsync();
}
```

