Consistency in method signatures is a good coding practice that ensures code reusability and stability of inheritance structures. Changing the 'params' modifier may cause misunderstandings about method functionality, leading to unexpected errors.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class Base
{
    public virtual void Foo(params object[] values)
    {
    }
}

public class Derived : Base
{
    public override void Foo(object[] values)
    {
    }
}
```

## Correct Example
