if (x ^ y)
{
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule suggests using the ^ operator in conditional expressions to replace complex logical comparisons, enhancing code readability and simplicity.

## Rule Meaning
In C#, the ^ operator performs a bitwise XOR. For boolean values, it returns true only if exactly one of the operands is true. Using the ^ operator can make conditional expressions clearer.

## Error Example
```csharp
if ((x && !y) || (!x && y))
{
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
if (x ^ y)
{
}
```

