## Rule Meaning
Boxing operations for value types cause new memory allocation on the heap and can lead to additional garbage collection, thus impacting program performance. Minimizing unnecessary boxing is recommended, especially in high-performance scenarios.

## Error Example
'''csharp
string s = null;
int i = 0;

// ...

string x = s + i;
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
string s = null;
int i = 0;

// ...

string x = s + i.ToString();
'''

