# 规则概述
在异步方法中直接返回`null`会导致潜在的运行时错误。此规则建议用已完成的任务(`Task.FromResult`)来替代返回`null`。

## 规则意义
这个规则的意义在于增强代码的健壮性和可移植性。在异步编程中，返回`null`可能导致`NullReferenceException`，而使用已完成的任务可以确保异步方法的调用一致性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
Task<object> GetAsync()
{
    return null;
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
Task<object> GetAsync()
{
    return Task.FromResult<object>(null);
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
Returning `null` in async methods can lead to potential runtime errors. This rule suggests returning a completed task using `Task.FromResult` instead of returning `null`.

## Rule Meaning
The significance of this rule lies in enhancing the robustness and portability of the code. In asynchronous programming, returning `null` can lead to `NullReferenceException`, while using a completed task ensures consistency in async method calls.

## Error Example
```csharp
Task<object> GetAsync()
{
    return null;
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
Task<object> GetAsync()
{
    return Task.FromResult<object>(null);
}
```

