# 规则概述
在实现 `IComparable<T>`、`IComparer<T>` 或 `IEqualityComparer<T>` 的公开类型时，建议同时实现它们的非泛型对应接口。

## 规则意义
C# 提供了泛型接口和非泛型接口，用以不同的比较或相等性需求。在实现泛型接口时，若不实现非泛型对应接口，可能导致在需要非泛型接口的场合出现不一致行为。因此，为确保类型的接口完整性和行为一致性，建议实现非泛型对应接口。

## 错误示例
```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class C
{
}

public abstract class Comparable : IComparable<C>
{
    public abstract int CompareTo(C other);
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class C
{
}

public abstract class Comparable : IComparable<C>, IComparable
{
    public abstract int CompareTo(C other);

    public int CompareTo(object obj)
    {
        if (obj == null)
        {
            return 1;
        }

        if (obj is C x)
        {
            return CompareTo(x);
        }

        throw new ArgumentException("", nameof(obj));
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
When implementing publicly visible types that implement `IComparable<T>`, `IComparer<T>`, or `IEqualityComparer<T>`, it is recommended to also implement their non-generic counterparts.

## Rule Meaning
C# provides both generic and non-generic interfaces for various comparison or equality operations. When implementing generic interfaces, failing to implement their non-generic counterparts can result in inconsistent behavior when non-generic interface usage is required. Hence, for ensuring interface completeness and consistent behavior of the type, it is advised to implement the non-generic counterparts.

## Error Example
```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class C
{
}

public abstract class Comparable : IComparable<C>
{
    public abstract int CompareTo(C other);
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class C
{
}

public abstract class Comparable : IComparable<C>, IComparable
{
    public abstract int CompareTo(C other);

    public int CompareTo(object obj)
    {
        if (obj == null)
        {
            return 1;
        }

        if (obj is C x)
        {
            return CompareTo(x);
        }

        throw new ArgumentException("", nameof(obj));
    }
}
```

