# 规则概述
此规则建议在判断集合是否为空或包含元素时，使用`Any()`方法代替使用`Count`属性，从而提高代码的可读性和潜在的性能表现。

## 规则意义
使用`Any()`方法可以让代码更加语义化，直接表明集合是否包含元素，同时在某些情况下可以避免遍历所有元素，仅判断是否存在任何元素，从而提高性能。

## 错误示例
```csharp
// 判断集合中是否有元素
if (syntaxList.Count > 0)
{
    // 处理逻辑
}

// 判断集合是否为空
if (syntaxList.Count == 0)
{
    // 处理逻辑
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
// 判断集合中是否有元素
if (syntaxList.Any())
{
    // 处理逻辑
}

// 判断集合是否为空
if (!syntaxList.Any())
{
    // 处理逻辑
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule suggests using the `Any()` method instead of the `Count` property when determining if a collection has elements or is empty, improving code readability and potential performance.

## Rule Meaning
Using the `Any()` method makes the code more semantic, directly indicating whether the collection has elements. In some cases, it can also avoid iterating over all elements, improving performance.

## Error Example
```csharp
// Check if collection has elements
if (syntaxList.Count > 0)
{
    // Processing logic
}

// Check if collection is empty
if (syntaxList.Count == 0)
{
    // Processing logic
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
// Check if collection has elements
if (syntaxList.Any())
{
    // Processing logic
}

// Check if collection is empty
if (!syntaxList.Any())
{
    // Processing logic
}
```

