if(condition){
    DoSomething();
}
else{
    DoSomethingElse();}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
if (condition) {
    DoSomething();
} else {
    DoSomethingElse();
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
SA1013 rule requires that closing braces ('}') in C# code should be styled with specific spacing. A closing brace should always be followed by a single space unless it is at the end of a line or followed by a closing parenthesis, comma, or semicolon. It should also be preceded by a single space unless it's the first character on the line.

## Rule Meaning
Following a consistent coding style improves code readability and maintainability, making it easier to understand and manage.

## Error Example
```csharp
if(condition){
    DoSomething();
}
else{
    DoSomethingElse();}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
if (condition) {
    DoSomething();
} else {
    DoSomethingElse();
}
```

