return (x.Value);
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
int x = 5 + b;
string y = this.Method().ToString();
return x.Value;
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In C#, parenthesis can be inserted around virtually any type of expression, statement, or clause, and in many situations, the use of parenthesis can greatly improve code readability. However, excessive use of parenthesis can have the opposite effect, making the code more difficult to read and maintain.

## Rule Meaning
The use of unnecessary parenthesis reduces code readability and increases maintenance costs. Avoiding unnecessary parenthesis helps to improve code neatness and readability.

## Error Example
```csharp
int x = (5 + b);
string y = (this.Method()).ToString();
return (x.Value);
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
int x = 5 + b;
string y = this.Method().ToString();
return x.Value;
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则要求在C#代码中，所有的注释必须包含实际的文本内容，而不能是空的。

## 规则意义
注释是代码中说明性的重要部分，帮助开发者理解代码逻辑。如果注释不包含任何文本，就失去了其存在的意义，容易导致混淆和误解。

## 错误示例
```csharp
//
// 
//TODO
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
// 这是一个有效的注释
// 解释代码的意图
//TODO: 完成此方法的实现
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that all comments in C# code must contain actual text content and not be empty.

## Rule Meaning
Comments are an important explanatory part of the code, helping developers understand the logic of the code. If a comment contains no text, it loses its meaning and can cause confusion and misunderstanding.

## Error Example
```csharp
//
// 
//TODO
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
// This is a valid comment
// Explains the intent of the code
//TODO: Complete the implementation of this method
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
使用C#内置类型时，应优先使用其内置类型别名而非类型名称或完全限定的类型名称。

## 规则意义
这种规范能够提高代码的可读性和一致性，使代码更简洁并且容易理解，因为大多数C#程序员对内置类型别名更为熟悉。

## 错误示例
```csharp
// 使用了完全限定的类型名称
System.Int32 number = 5;

// 使用了类型名称
