```

## 正确示例
```csharp
// 使用内置类型别名
int number = 5;

// 使用内置类型别名
int anotherNumber = 10;
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
When using C# built-in types, the built-in type alias should be used instead of the type name or the fully qualified type name.

## Rule Meaning
This guideline improves code readability and consistency by making the code more concise and easier to understand, as most C# developers are more familiar with the built-in type aliases.

## Error Example
```csharp
// Using fully qualified type name
System.Int32 number = 5;

// Using type name
Int32 anotherNumber = 10;
