rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则要求使用Lambda表达式语法替代匿名方法语法。这可以提高代码的可读性和简洁性。

## 规则意义
使用Lambda表达式可以使代码更加简洁，并且当用Lambda表达式时，代码通常更易于理解。与旧语法相比，Lambda语法更现代，更符合当前的代码风格惯例。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
Action a = delegate { x = 0; };
Action b = delegate() { y = 0; };
Func<int, int, int> c = delegate(int m, int n) { return m + n; };
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
Action a = () => { x = 0; };
Action b = () => { y = 0; };
Func<int, int, int> c = (m, n) => m + n;
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires using Lambda expression syntax instead of anonymous method syntax. It improves the readability and conciseness of the code.

## Rule Meaning
Using Lambda expressions makes the code more concise, and with Lambda syntax, the code is typically easier to understand. Compared to the old syntax, Lambda syntax is more modern and aligns more with current coding style conventions.

## Error Example
'''csharp
Action a = delegate { x = 0; };
Action b = delegate() { y = 0; };
Func<int, int, int> c = delegate(int m, int n) { return m + n; };
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
Action a = () => { x = 0; };
Action b = () => { y = 0; };
Func<int, int, int> c = (m, n) => m + n;
'''

rules.content:
# 规则概述
在代码中，比较运算的可读性对于后续的代码维护非常重要。当比较操作涉及文字或常量值与变量值时，常见的可读性问题是将变量放在表达式的右侧。

## 规则意义
在条件表达式中，将变量放在左侧能够提高代码的可读性和一致性，有助于减少错误的发生，增强代码的可维护性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public void Method(string value)
{
    if (null == value) // SA1131
    {
        throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(value));
    }
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public void Method(string value)
{
    if (value == null)
    {
        throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(value));
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In code, the readability of comparison operations is crucial for subsequent code maintenance. When a comparison involves a literal or constant value and a variable value, a common readability issue is placing the variable on the right-hand side of the expression.

## Rule Meaning
Placing the variable on the left side of the conditional expression can improve code readability and consistency, help reduce errors, and enhance code maintainability.

## Error Example
```csharp
public void Method(string value)
{
    if (null == value) // SA1131
    {
        throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(value));
    }
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public void Method(string value)
{
    if (value == null)
    {
        throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(value));
    }
}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
在C#语言的编程中，应避免在同一个字段定义中声明多个字段。这有助于提高代码的可读性和维护性。

## 规则意义
通过强制每个字段在其自己的定义中声明，代码变得更明确和易于阅读。这也有助于减少可能因多行字段声明而导致的错误。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
public class TypeName
{
    private int field1,
        field2; // SA1132
}
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
public class TypeName
{
    private int field1;
    private int field2;
}
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In C# programming, multiple fields should not be declared in the same field definition. This helps to improve code readability and maintainability.

## Rule Meaning
By enforcing that each field is declared in its own definition, the code becomes clearer and easier to read. It also helps to minimize errors that might occur due to multiline field declarations.

## Error Example
'''csharp
public class TypeName
{
    private int field1,
        field2; // SA1132
}
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
public class TypeName
{
    private int field1;
    private int field2;
}
'''

rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则要求当使用指令位于命名空间内时，必须使用完整的命名空间名称。

## 规则意义
不使用完整命名空间名称可能会导致代码可读性降低，并且可能引起命名冲突的问题。通过使用全限定的命名空间名称，可以明确引用的类型来源，增加代码的可维护性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
namespace System.Threading
{
    using IO;
    using Tasks;
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
namespace System.Threading
{
    using System.IO;
    using System.Threading.Tasks;

    using T = Thread;
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that when a using directive is within a namespace, the full namespace name must be used.

## Rule Meaning
Not using fully qualified namespace names can reduce code readability and may lead to naming conflicts. By using fully qualified names, the origin of a type is clearer, which improves code maintainability.

## Error Example
```csharp
namespace System.Threading
{
    using IO;
    using Tasks;
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
namespace System.Threading
{
    using System.IO;
    using System.Threading.Tasks;

    using T = Thread;
}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则检查位于同一级别的代码元素是否具有一致的缩进。例如，在同一个代码块中的两个方法调用需要有相同的缩进，以提高代码的可读性。

## 规则意义
保持代码缩进的一致性可以提高代码的可读性，使得开发人员能够更容易地理解代码结构和意图。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
public void MethodName()
{
    A();
   B(); // SA1137: 期望缩进与上一行匹配
}
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
public void MethodName()
{
    A();
    B();
}
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule checks if code elements at the same level have consistent indentation. For example, two method calls within the same code block need to be indented the same to enhance readability.

## Rule Meaning
Maintaining consistent indentation in code enhances readability, making it easier for developers to understand the code structure and intent.

## Error Example
'''csharp
public void MethodName()
{
    A();
   B(); // SA1137: Expected the indentation to match the previous line
}
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
public void MethodName()
{
    A();
    B();
}
'''

rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则要求C#的using指令必须放置在命名空间元素内部，除非文件不包含任何命名空间。

## 规则意义
在命名空间内放置using指令有助于消除编译器在冲突类型之间的混淆，并且在单个文件中定义多个命名空间时，使引用和别名的作用域更加明确。

