namespace Microsoft.Sample
{
    using System;
    using Guid = System.Guid;

    public class Program
    {
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that C# using directives must be placed inside a namespace element unless the file does not contain any namespace elements.

## Rule Meaning
Placing using directives within the namespace element helps eliminate compiler confusion between conflicting types and scopes references and aliases when multiple namespaces are defined within a single file.

