rules.content:
# 规则概述
在C#代码文件中，代码元素应该按照标准顺序排列，以提高代码的可读性和可维护性。这条规则要求文件根级别或命名空间内部的元素按特定顺序排列。

## 规则意义
遵循标准的排序方案有助于提高文件的可读性和可维护性，鼓励代码复用。通过统一的代码结构，新成员在加入代码库时，能够更快地理解代码结构。

## 错误示例
```csharp
using System;

namespace Example
{
    public class MyClass
    {
        public void MyMethod() {}
        private int myField;
    }
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
using System;

namespace Example
{
    public class MyClass
    {
        private int myField;
        public void MyMethod() {}
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In a C# code file, code elements should be arranged in a standard order to improve code readability and maintainability. This rule requires elements at the file root level or within a namespace to be positioned in a specific sequence.

## Rule Meaning
Complying with a standard ordering scheme can enhance the readability and maintainability of the file and encourage code reuse. A unified code structure helps new members understand the codebase more quickly.

## Error Example
```csharp
using System;

namespace Example
{
    public class MyClass
    {
        public void MyMethod() {}
        private int myField;
    }
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
using System;

namespace Example
{
    public class MyClass
    {
        private int myField;
        public void MyMethod() {}
    }
}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
在C#代码文件中，根据访问级别进行标准排序的元素没有被正确排序时，会违反此规则。

## 规则意义
按照访问级别的标准排序方案，可以提高文件的可读性和可维护性，并且更容易识别类所公开的公共接口。

## 错误示例
```csharp
private void MethodA() {}
public void MethodB() {}
protected void MethodC() {}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public void MethodB() {}
protected void MethodC() {}
private void MethodA() {}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
A violation of this rule occurs when the code elements within a file do not follow a standard ordering scheme based on access level.

## Rule Meaning
Complying with a standard ordering scheme based on access level can increase the readability and maintainability of the file and make it easier to identify the public interface that is being exposed from a class.

## Error Example
```csharp
private void MethodA() {}
public void MethodB() {}
protected void MethodC() {}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public void MethodB() {}
protected void MethodC() {}
private void MethodA() {}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则要求在C#代码中，所有常量字段必须出现在非常量字段之前。

## 规则意义
将常量放在非常量字段之前可以清晰地传达这些元素在编译器的处理方式、命名要求等方面的不同。这种排列方式有助于提高代码的可读性和维护性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int exampleField;
    private const int ExampleConstant = 10;
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private const int ExampleConstant = 10;
    private int exampleField;
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that in C# code, all constant fields must appear before non-constant fields.

## Rule Meaning
Placing constants before non-constant fields clearly communicates the different considerations for the compiler and naming requirements. This arrangement improves code readability and maintainability.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int exampleField;
    private const int ExampleConstant = 10;
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private const int ExampleConstant = 10;
    private int exampleField;
}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
在C#类中，静态元素应位于相同类型的实例元素之前，以提高代码可读性和可维护性。

## 规则意义
将静态元素排列在实例元素之前可以使类接口更为直观，有助于开发者快速了解类的静态方法及属性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    public void InstanceMethod() {}
    public static void StaticMethod() {}
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    public static void StaticMethod() {}
    public void InstanceMethod() {}
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In a C# class, static elements should appear before instance elements of the same type to enhance code readability and maintainability.

## Rule Meaning
Arranging static elements before instance elements provides a clearer view of the class interface, aiding developers in quickly understanding the static methods and properties of the class.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    public void InstanceMethod() {}
    public static void StaticMethod() {}
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    public static void StaticMethod() {}
    public void InstanceMethod() {}
}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
在C#中，部分元素可以被多个文件定义，但需要统一的访问修饰符。此规则要求所有部分元素必须声明访问修饰符，以确保代码的可读性和一致性。

## 规则意义
指定访问修饰符有助于明确元素的可访问性，防止程序员误解代码的意图，也有助于维护和扩展代码。

## 错误示例
```csharp
partial class MyClass
{
    void MyMethod() { }
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public partial class MyClass
{
    public void MyMethod() { }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In C#, partial elements can be defined across multiple files, but they need a unified access modifier. This rule requires all partial elements to declare an access modifier, ensuring code readability and consistency.

## Rule Meaning
Specifying an access modifier helps clarify the accessibility of elements, preventing misunderstandings about the code's intent, and facilitates code maintenance and extension.

## Error Example
```csharp
partial class MyClass
{
    void MyMethod() { }
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public partial class MyClass
{
    public void MyMethod() { }
}
```

