# 规则概述
在C#语言中，*protected*和*internal*修饰词可以同时用于定义成员的访问级别。为了代码的可读性和一致性，StyleCop规范要求修饰词的顺序应该是固定的，即在使用*protected internal*时，*protected*应放在*internal*之前，而在使用*private protected*时，*private*应放在*protected*之前。

## 规则意义
正确的修饰词顺序可以避免混淆，提高代码的统一性和可读性。此外，保持风格的一致性有助于团队协作，减少误解。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
public class Example
{
    internal protected int incorrectOrder;
    protected private void AnotherIncorrectOrder() {}
}
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
public class Example
{
    protected internal int correctOrder;
    private protected void AnotherCorrectOrder() {}
}
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In the C# language, the *protected* and *internal* modifiers can be used together to define the access level of members. StyleCop standardizes the order of these modifiers for the sake of readability and consistency, requiring that the *protected* keyword precedes the *internal* keyword when using *protected internal*, and the *private* keyword precedes the *protected* keyword when using *private protected*.

## Rule Meaning
Correct ordering of modifiers helps avoid confusion, improves code uniformity and readability. Consistent styling aids in team collaboration and reduces misunderstandings.

## Error Example
'''csharp
public class Example
{
    internal protected int incorrectOrder;
    protected private void AnotherIncorrectOrder() {}
}
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
public class Example
{
    protected internal int correctOrder;
    private protected void AnotherCorrectOrder() {}
}
'''

