# 规则概述
在C#代码中，using别名指令可以影响文件或命名空间中代码的含义。因此，将using别名指令放在所有其他using指令之后，可以使代码更整洁、更易读，同时有助于识别代码中使用的类型。

## 规则意义
遵循此规则可以提高代码可读性和维护性，通过明确命名空间别名的定义顺序，避免潜在含义冲突。

## 错误示例
'''csharp
using MyAlias = System.Text;
using System;

class Sample
{
    // ... 代码内容
}
'''

## 正确示例
'''csharp
using System;
using MyAlias = System.Text;

class Sample
{
    // ... 代码内容
}
'''

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In C# code, using-alias directives can affect the meaning of the code within the file or namespace. Placing using-alias directives after all other using directives can make the code cleaner and easier to read, and help in identifying the types used throughout the code.

## Rule Meaning
Adhering to this rule enhances code readability and maintainability, ensuring clear order in namespace alias definitions and avoiding potential meaning conflicts.

## Error Example
'''csharp
using MyAlias = System.Text;
using System;

class Sample
{
    // ... code content
}
'''

## Correct Example
'''csharp
using System;
using MyAlias = System.Text;

class Sample
{
    // ... code content
}
'''

