# 规则概述
此规则要求C#代码文件中的using指令必须按照命名空间字母顺序排列。System命名空间除外，需置于其他命名空间之前。

## 规则意义
按字母顺序排列using指令可以使代码更整洁，便于阅读，并且有助于快速识别代码中使用的命名空间。

## 错误示例
```csharp
using Microsoft.CodeAnalysis;
using System.Linq;
using System;
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
using System;
using System.Linq;
using Microsoft.CodeAnalysis;
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that using directives in a C# code file must be ordered alphabetically by namespace. The System namespaces are an exception and should come first before other namespaces.

## Rule Meaning
Ordering using directives alphabetically makes the code cleaner, easier to read, and helps quickly identify the namespaces used in the code.

## Error Example
```csharp
using Microsoft.CodeAnalysis;
using System.Linq;
using System;
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
using System;
using System.Linq;
using Microsoft.CodeAnalysis;
```

