# 规则概述
此规则要求`using static`指令必须放置在普通`using`指令之后，别名`using`指令之前。这有助于提高代码的可读性和维护性。

## 规则意义
通过将`using static`指令放置在适当的位置，可以使代码更清晰，更易于阅读，并且更容易识别代码中使用的静态成员。

## 错误示例
```csharp
using static System.Math;
using System.IO;
using MyAlias = System.Collections.Generic;
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
using System.IO;
using static System.Math;
using MyAlias = System.Collections.Generic;
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that `using static` directives be placed after regular `using` directives and before alias `using` directives. This helps improve code readability and maintainability.

## Rule Meaning
By placing `using static` directives in the correct location, the code becomes clearer, easier to read, and static members used throughout the code become easier to identify.

## Error Example
```csharp
using static System.Math;
using System.IO;
using MyAlias = System.Collections.Generic;
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
using System.IO;
using static System.Math;
using MyAlias = System.Collections.Generic;
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则要求在C#代码文件中，`using static`指令必须按完整类型名称的字母顺序排列。

## 规则意义
按字母顺序排列`using static`指令可以使代码更加整洁，并提高可读性。这种排序规则有助于开发者快速定位并管理代码中的静态引用。

## 错误示例
```csharp
using static System.Console;
using static System.Math;
using static System.Collections.Generic.List<int>;
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
using static System.Collections.Generic.List<int>;
using static System.Console;
using static System.Math;
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that `using static` directives within a C# code file must be ordered alphabetically by full type name.

## Rule Meaning
Ordering `using static` directives alphabetically makes the code cleaner and easier to read. This practice helps developers quickly locate and manage static references in the code.

## Error Example
```csharp
using static System.Console;
using static System.Math;
using static System.Collections.Generic.List<int>;
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
using static System.Collections.Generic.List<int>;
using static System.Console;
