# 规则概述
此规则要求某些C#元素的名称必须以大写字母开头。这是为了确保代码的一致性和可读性。

## 规则意义
以大写字母开头的名称遵循了C#语言的命名惯例，能够提高代码的可读性和专业性，也有助于避免潜在的命名冲突。

## 错误示例
```csharp
namespace exampleNamespace // 名称不以大写开头
{
    public class exampleClass // 名称不以大写开头
    {
        public void doSomething() // 名称不以大写开头
        {
        }
    }
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
namespace ExampleNamespace // 名称以大写开头
{
    public class ExampleClass // 名称以大写开头
    {
        public void DoSomething() // 名称以大写开头
        {
        }
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that certain C# elements must begin with an upper-case letter. This is to ensure consistency and readability in the code.

## Rule Meaning
Names that begin with an upper-case letter follow the naming conventions of the C# language, improving readability and professionalism in the code and helping to avoid potential naming conflicts.

## Error Example
```csharp
namespace exampleNamespace // Name does not begin with upper-case
{
    public class exampleClass // Name does not begin with upper-case
    {
        public void doSomething() // Name does not begin with upper-case
        {
        }
    }
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
namespace ExampleNamespace // Name begins with upper-case
{
    public class ExampleClass // Name begins with upper-case
    {
        public void DoSomething() // Name begins with upper-case
        {
        }
    }
}
```

