# 规则概述
SA1301规则要求C#代码中的元素名称必须以小写字母开头，以确保代码风格的一致性和可读性。

## 规则意义
遵循命名约定不仅可以提高代码的可读性和可维护性，还能使团队协作更为顺畅。此外，一致的命名风格可以避免潜在的命名冲突或语义误解。

## 错误示例
```csharp
class SampleClass
{
    private int IncorrectName;

    public void Method()
    {
        int LocalVariable = 0;
    }
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
class SampleClass
{
    private int correctName;

    public void Method()
    {
        int localVariable = 0;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
The SA1301 rule requires that element names in C# code must begin with a lowercase letter to ensure consistency and readability of the code style.

## Rule Meaning
Following naming conventions not only enhances the readability and maintainability of the code but also facilitates smoother teamwork. Additionally, a consistent naming style can prevent potential naming conflicts or semantic misunderstandings.

## Error Example
```csharp
class SampleClass
{
    private int IncorrectName;

    public void Method()
    {
        int LocalVariable = 0;
    }
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
class SampleClass
{
    private int correctName;

    public void Method()
    {
        int localVariable = 0;
    }
}
```

