# 规则概述
该规则强制要求C#字段名称以小写字母开头，从而提高代码的一致性和可读性。在C#中，私有的只读字段应该以小写字母开头，而常量、非私有的只读字段和静态只读字段应以大写字母开头。对于公有或内部字段，应该始终以大写字母开头。

## 规则意义
使用一致的命名约定有助于避免在代码中引入歧义和错误，从而提高团队间的代码可维护性和可读性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int InvalidFieldName;
    public int PublicFieldName;
    private readonly int ReadOnlyFieldName;
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int validFieldName;
    public int PublicFieldName;
    private readonly int readOnlyFieldName;
    public const int ConstantFieldName = 10;
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires field names in C# to begin with a lower-case letter to ensure consistency and readability. Private readonly fields should start with a lower-case letter, while constants, non-private readonly fields, and static readonly fields should begin with an upper-case letter. Public or internal fields should always start with an upper-case letter.

## Rule Meaning
Consistent naming conventions help avoid ambiguity and errors in code, thereby improving maintainability and readability across teams.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int InvalidFieldName;
    public int PublicFieldName;
    private readonly int ReadOnlyFieldName;
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int validFieldName;
    public int PublicFieldName;
    private readonly int readOnlyFieldName;
    public const int ConstantFieldName = 10;
}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
