# 规则概述
SA1308 规则定义了在 C# 编码中，字段名称不应以* m_ *、* s_ *或* t_ *作为前缀。为了提升代码可读性和一致性，建议使用 'this.' 前缀。

## 规则意义
使用 'this.' 前缀而不是下划线前缀有助于在所有元素类型（包括方法、属性等）中统一调用类成员。此外，它可以直观地区分实例成员和静态成员，后者无需前缀。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int m_value; // 错误：字段名称以 m_ 前缀开头
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int value;

    public void SetValue(int value)
    {
        this.value = value; // 使用 'this.' 前缀来区分成员变量
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
SA1308 defines that field names in C# should not be prefixed by *m_*, *s_*, or *t_*. To enhance readability and consistency, it is suggested to use the 'this.' prefix.

## Rule Meaning
Using the 'this.' prefix instead of underscores helps in uniformly calling class members across all element types, including methods and properties. Additionally, it provides a clear distinction between instance members and static members, the latter of which are not prefixed.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int m_value; // Error: Field name starts with prefix m_
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int value;

    public void SetValue(int value)
    {
        this.value = value; // Use 'this.' prefix to differentiate instance member
    }
}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
在C#中，字段名称不应以下划线开头。StyleCop默认不允许使用下划线或诸如'm_'等前缀标记类的字段，建议使用'this.'前缀。这样做的好处是对所有元素类型都适用，包括方法、属性等，能在任何代码编辑器中使类成员的调用立即可识别。此外，它还能帮助快速识别实例成员和静态成员，因为静态成员不会有前缀。

## 规则意义
使用'this.'前缀能够保证代码的一致性和可读性，同时避免可能与开发工具产生的混淆。如果一个字段或变量名称需要与Win32或COM相关的项目匹配，需要以下划线开头，则应将该字段或变量放在一个以NativeMethods结尾的特殊类中，以便StyleCop忽略此违规。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    private int _myField;
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    private int myField;

    public void Method()
    {
        this.myField = 10;
    }
}
```

或者使用NativeMethods类：

```csharp
public class MyNativeMethods
{
    private int _myField;
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In C#, field names should not begin with an underscore. By default, StyleCop disallows underscores or prefixes like 'm_' for marking class fields, recommending the use of the 'this.' prefix. The advantage is that 'this.' applies to all element types, including methods and properties, making member calls instantly recognizable in any code editor. It also creates a quick distinction between instance members and static members, as static members will not be prefixed.

## Rule Meaning
Using the 'this.' prefix ensures code consistency and readability while avoiding potential confusion that may arise with development tools. If a field or variable name needs to match the name of an item associated with Win32 or COM and thus needs to begin with an underscore, place the field within a special class with a name ending in NativeMethods to make StyleCop ignore the violation.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    private int _myField;
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    private int myField;

    public void Method()
    {
        this.myField = 10;
    }
}
```

Or using a NativeMethods class:

```csharp
public class MyNativeMethods
{
    private int _myField;
}
```

