# 规则概述
SA1401规则要求C#类中的字段应被定义为私有，以确保类的可维护性和封装性。在类中使用属性，而不是公开字段，可以方便地改变内部实现而不影响类的接口。

## 规则意义
对外暴露字段会使类的接口变得不稳定，增加了维护的难度。使用私有字段和公共属性的方式能够在未来更改实现时保持接口不变，提升代码的可维护性。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    public int exampleField; // 不推荐的做法，字段是公共的
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int exampleField;

    public int ExampleField
    {
        get { return exampleField; }
        set { exampleField = value; }
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
SA1401 rule mandates that fields in a C# class should be private to enhance maintainability and encapsulation. Properties should be used to expose fields externally, allowing internal implementation changes without altering the class interface.

## Rule Meaning
Exposing fields directly can lead to interface instability, making maintenance difficult. Using private fields and public properties allows for implementation changes without modifying the interface, improving code maintainability.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    public int exampleField; // Discouraged practice, the field is public
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private int exampleField;

    public int ExampleField
    {
        get { return exampleField; }
        set { exampleField = value; }
    }
}
```

