# 规则概述
本规则要求源代码文件使用 UTF-8 含字节顺序标记（BOM）的编码格式进行存储。

## 规则意义
使用统一的 UTF-8 编码格式可以确保文件在不同操作系统及编译器设置下被一致解析。这也提高了文件在 GitHub 等平台上进行视觉差异分析的支持度，并且是 Visual Studio 创建新文件时的默认编码。

## 错误示例
```csharp
// 假设文件使用非 UTF-8 编码保存
// 这段代码没有明显的错误，但由于编码问题可能在不同系统上出现问题
Console.WriteLine("你好，世界！");
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
// 文件使用 UTF-8 含 BOM 编码保存
Console.WriteLine("你好，世界！");
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires source code files to be stored in UTF-8 encoding with byte order mark (BOM).

## Rule Meaning
Using a uniform UTF-8 encoding ensures that files are processed consistently across different operating systems and compiler settings. It also enhances support for visual diffs on platforms like GitHub and is the default encoding when creating new files in Visual Studio.

## Error Example
```csharp
// Assume the file is saved in a non-UTF-8 encoding
// This code does not have obvious errors, but may cause issues on different systems due to encoding
Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
// The file is saved in UTF-8 with BOM encoding
Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
```

