rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In C# code, when a statement, element, or expression contains braces, the opening and closing braces must each be placed on their own line.

## Rule Meaning
This rule helps improve code readability and consistency, making the code style uniform, easier to maintain, and understand.

## Error Example
