# 规则概述
在C#语言中，某些语句允许省略花括号，如`if`、`while`和`for`语句。本规则要求所有代码块必须使用花括号，以提高代码的可读性和可维护性。

## 规则意义
省略花括号容易导致错误。例如，当在没有花括号的`if`语句下插入其他语句时，乍一看可能会误以为两个语句都是`if`语句的子句，实际情况却并非如此。这种误解可能会引发错误。

## 错误示例
```csharp
if (true) 
    this.value = 2;       
    return this.value;
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
if (true) 
{
    this.value = 2;
    return this.value;
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
In C#, some statements allow braces to be omitted, such as `if`, `while`, and `for` statements. This rule requires that all code blocks must include braces in order to enhance the readability and maintainability of the code.

## Rule Meaning
Omitting braces can easily lead to errors. For example, when inserting another statement under an `if` statement without braces, it may appear that both statements are children of the `if` statement, but in fact, they are not. This misunderstanding can introduce bugs.

## Error Example
```csharp
if (true) 
    this.value = 2;       
    return this.value;
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
if (true) 
{
    this.value = 2;
    return this.value;
}
```

