# 规则概述
为提高代码的可读性，StyleCop要求在特定情况下使用空行，而在其他情况下禁止使用空行。这形成了一种一致的视觉模式，可以提高对不熟悉代码的识别性和可读性。

## 规则意义
某些C#语句类型只能作为其他语句的补充部分来使用。例子包括`catch`和`finally`语句，这些语句必须始终与`try`语句连在一起。另一个例子是`else`语句，它必须与`if`语句或另一个`else`语句连在一起。这样的链式语句不应以空行分隔。

## 错误示例
```csharp
try
{
    this.SomeMethod();
}

catch (Exception ex)
{
    Console.WriteLine(ex.ToString());
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
try
{
    this.SomeMethod();
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    Console.WriteLine(ex.ToString());
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
To improve the readability of the code, StyleCop requires blank lines in certain situations, and prohibits blank lines in others. This results in a consistent visual pattern across the code, which can improve recognition and readability of unfamiliar code.

## Rule Meaning
Some types of C# statements can only be used when chained to the bottom of another statement. Examples include `catch` and `finally` statements, which must always be chained to the bottom of a `try`-statement. Another example is an `else`-statement, which must always be chained to the bottom of an `if`-statement, or to another `else`-statement. These types of chained statements should not be separated by a blank line.

## Error Example
```csharp
try
{
    this.SomeMethod();
}

catch (Exception ex)
{
    Console.WriteLine(ex.ToString());
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
try
{
    this.SomeMethod();
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    Console.WriteLine(ex.ToString());
}
```

