Documenting code improves readability and maintainability. For partial classes, to ensure consistency in SDK documentation, it is advisable to use the `<summary>` tag for official SDK documentation on the main part of the class while replacing it with the `<content>` tag for other parts. This rule requires documentation for each part of the class to enhance code readability and maintainability.

