# 规则概述
此规则确保在类或接口元素上使用`<inheritdoc>`时，该元素必须从基类继承或实现接口。若元素不具备继承关系却使用了`<inheritdoc>`，则会违反此规则。

## 规则意义
使用`<inheritdoc>`可以有效复用文档注释，提高代码可读性和可维护性。然而，只有在确实存在继承关系时使用才有意义，否则应单独对该元素进行注释。

## 错误示例
```csharp
/// <inheritdoc/>
public class MyClass
{
    // 没有继承自基类或接口
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
/// <inheritdoc/>
public class MyDerivedClass : MyBaseClass
{
    // 继承自MyBaseClass
}

/// <inheritdoc cref="IMyInterface"/>
public class MyClass : IMyInterface
{
    // 实现了接口IMyInterface
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule ensures that the `<inheritdoc>` element is used only on elements that inherit from a base class or implement an interface. A violation of this rule occurs when an element uses `<inheritdoc>` without inheriting from a base class or implementing an interface.

## Rule Meaning
Using `<inheritdoc>` allows for effective reuse of documentation comments, improving the readability and maintainability of the code. However, it only makes sense to use it when there is an actual inheritance relationship; otherwise, the element should be documented separately.

## Error Example
```csharp
/// <inheritdoc/>
public class MyClass
{
    // Does not inherit from a base class or interface
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
/// <inheritdoc/>
public class MyDerivedClass : MyBaseClass
{
    // Inherits from MyBaseClass
}

/// <inheritdoc cref="IMyInterface"/>
public class MyClass : IMyInterface
{
    // Implements the interface IMyInterface
}
```

