## 错误示例
```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    private int fieldValue;
    public MyClass(int value)
    {
        fieldValue = value;
    }
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    private int _fieldValue;
    public MyClass(int value)
    {
        _fieldValue = value;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that all field names must begin with an underscore (_). Adhering to this naming convention helps differentiate fields from other variables such as method parameters and local variables, thereby enhancing code readability. Following a uniform naming convention makes the fields in the code apparent at a glance and reduces the risk of naming conflicts.

## Rule Meaning
Maintaining a consistent field naming convention enhances code maintainability, readability, and consistency, aiding team members in quickly understanding the code structure.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    private int fieldValue;
    public MyClass(int value)
    {
        fieldValue = value;
    }
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    private int _fieldValue;
    public MyClass(int value)
    {
        _fieldValue = value;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
# 规则概述
此规则要求所有静态字段名称必须以下划线(`_`)开头。这有助于在代码中快速识别静态字段，提高代码可读性和维护性。

## 规则意义
遵循一致的命名约定可以增强代码的可读性和可维护性。静态字段由于其全局性的特征，使用下划线开头可以帮助区分它们与普通成员变量。

## 错误示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private static int staticValue = 10;
}
```

## 正确示例
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private static int _staticValue = 10;
}
```

rules.content_en:
# Rule Overview
This rule requires that all static field names must begin with an underscore (`_`). This helps in quickly identifying static fields within the code, thereby improving readability and maintainability.

## Rule Meaning
Following consistent naming conventions can enhance code readability and maintainability. Since static fields have a global presence, starting their names with an underscore helps distinguish them from regular member variables.

## Error Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private static int staticValue = 10;
}
```

## Correct Example
```csharp
public class ExampleClass
{
    private static int _staticValue = 10;
}
```
